  "lineage": "Parisian dance-hall music of the 1880s-1930s, begun in Auvergnat immigrant bals of the Bastille and Italie quarters where the bellows-blown cabrette bagpipe led bourrées, then reshaped after 1900 as Italian immigrant accordionists took over and standardised the repertoire of valse, java, polka and paso doble in fast 3/4 and 2/4, played by accordion with banjo and drums for a paying, close-packed dancing crowd.",
